WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:02.280
Over the love-hateyears,

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:07.480
I've had a love-hate relationship
with I-cord edging for my knitting.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.160
Sometimes it looks good.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:18.040
And other times, not so much.
So I often will turn to crochet.

5
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.640
Now, I recently discovered why. I've never

6
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.920
paid attention to the direction
that I'm slipping.

7
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.000
OK, let's start at the beginning.

8
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:36.280
I-cord is created by casting on a few
stitches and knitting in one direction.

9
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.400
And slipping in the other.

10
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:48.240
By carrying the working yarn
with the slip and I-cord forms.

11
00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.680
You can create a finished edge for your

12
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.200
knitting by joining the edge
of your knitting to some I-cord.

13
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.960
Pick up the edge loops and hang them one
at a time on the end needle of the cord.

14
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.520
And knit cord and edge
strand together to join.

15
00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.360
Here's my big discovery. In this example,

16
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.680
I'm slipping to the left.

17
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:18.400
I'll pick up the edge
loop and join my I-cord.

18
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.960
It creates a beautiful edge.

19
00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.640
Looks great on both sides.

20
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.360
Next, I'll reverse the slip setting.

21
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:34.360
I'm still picking up along the left hand
edge here, but I am slipping to the right.

22
00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.880
Now, it may be difficult to see in these

23
00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.960
images, but there is quite a bit
of difference between the two methods.

24
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:06.080
My I-cord join is so much better when I
slip in the direction that I'm picking up.

25
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.680
Mystery solved.

26
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.640
I may just start using I-cord again.

27
00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.280
Now, if you don't believe me,
give it a try.

28
00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.960
You may be as surprised as I was.

